# Returns the full path of the scratch library, always.
# Without pPathOnly_opt it also makes sure the library is OPEN, creating
# it when the file is gone.
#
# The path is built HERE and nowhere else. $resetScratch asks for it with
# pPathOnly_opt, so the logic exists exactly once.
#
# Do not open startup task: a class that accidentally becomes the startup
# task of a scratch library must not run when the library is opened.
# Internal name given explicitly - Omnis would otherwise derive it from the
# file name, uppercased on Windows.

Calculate scratchName as 'execScratch'
Calculate scratchPath as con(mid(sys(10),1,rpos(sys(9),sys(10))),scratchName,'.lbs')
If pPathOnly_opt
	Quit method scratchPath
End If
If $root.$libs.$findname(scratchName)
	Quit method scratchPath
End If
If FileOps.$doesfileexist(scratchPath)
	Open library (Do not close others,Do not open startup task) [scratchPath],[scratchName]
Else
	Create library (Do not close others) [scratchPath],[scratchName]
	# Create library puts an EMPTY Startup_Task into EVERY new library (2026-09-24). Here it would start when
	# the scratch is opened through the Studio Browser, and make the bare name Startup_Task ambiguous.
	Set reference libRef to $root.$libs.$findname(scratchName)
	If not(isclear(libRef.$classes.$findname('Startup_Task')))
		Do libRef.$classes.$remove(libRef.$classes.$findname('Startup_Task').$ref)
	End If
End If
Quit method scratchPath